# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file. go.work is committed: it declares the sibling
# declarative-agents checkout the development loop builds against, and go.mod
# carries the pin that GOWORK=off resolves instead (GH-110). Its checksum file
# stays local.
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# --- cohere-demo additions ---

# Compiled mage/orchestrator binaries
bin/
/build/

# Local credentials, never committed (the tooling reads these at runtime). No
# trailing slash: the path is a symlink here, and a trailing slash matches only
# directories, which left the link showing as untracked.
.secrets

# Chatbot SPA dependencies. The built bundle agents/chatbot/ui/app/dist IS
# committed and must stay tracked; only node_modules is ignored.
**/node_modules/

# Local observability run state (Prometheus/Grafana scratch)
observability/.run/

# Rendered Helm output
helm/dist/
# The agent-services library chart, vendored from the pinned release.
helm/charts/

# orchestrator.go init() writes this when run from magefiles/ (e.g. go test ./magefiles/);
# the tracked configuration.yaml lives at the repo root.
magefiles/configuration.yaml

# The rel10.5 source datasets (data/) are 343MB of harvested reporting held
# outside version control: the corpus build reads them, the store it writes is
# what the repository carries. They are ignored rather than merely untracked
# because `git add -A` would otherwise stage the whole 343MB, and the failure
# is one command away from a commit nobody wants to undo.
#
# The per-tier READMEs are the exception. They record each tier's source,
# licence, and retrieval date (srd017 R9.2), which is the part that has to
# travel with the repository rather than with the data.
/data/**
!/data/
!/data/*/
!/data/*/README.md

# The keep-private store tiers (srd017 R9.7, GH-910) are versioned in the
# private mesh-intelligence/cohere-demo-data repository, never here. The build
# writes them into that checkout, so these rules are defense in depth against a
# misconfigured run leaving copyrighted chunks where `git add -A` would stage
# them; corpus_dataset_ignore_test.go asserts the rules hold.
/corpus/store/documents/isw-*/
/corpus/store/documents/tg-*/
/corpus/store/documents/losses-*/
/corpus/store/documents/missile-*/

# Evaluation run artifacts (srd014): reports are run outputs, not repo content.
evaluation/report.json
talks/.obsidian/
.claude
.cursor

# Local GCP operator configuration (gcp:deploy); it names a real project.
gcp.yaml

# Terraform working directories and the bootstrap root's local state (infra/gcp).
infra/gcp/**/.terraform/
infra/gcp/bootstrap/terraform.tfstate*

# The operator contact a case's fetch declares to the SEC (srd018 R2.6).
cases/*/fetch.local.yaml
